return array (
  'content' => '<p>A metal coffee table anchors the living room seating group — scale, finish and top material signal the interior\'s ambition before anyone sits down. In Indian luxury homes, PVD stainless bases with stone or glass tops bridge architectural metalwork from entrance and partitions into furnished comfort.</p><h2>Scale relative to sofa and room</h2><p>Table length often ½ to ⅔ of sofa length; height typically 400–450 mm to match seat cushion level. Oversized tables dominate compact Mumbai living rooms; undersized look lost in Gurgaon villa lounges.</p><p>Leave 450–500 mm clearance between table edge and sofa for passage — tighter in small flats.</p><h2>Base design and visual weight</h2><p>Sculptural PVD bases in champagne or black create focal points on neutral rugs. Minimal frame bases suit rooms already rich in pattern — marble floors, feature walls.</p><p>Browse <a href="/shop/coffee-tables">coffee tables</a> and custom options on <a href="/shop/bespoke-metal-furniture">bespoke metal furniture</a>.</p><h2>Top materials</h2><p><strong>Marble and quartzite</strong> — popular in North India; book-match for statement.</p><p><strong>Tempered glass</strong> — light visual weight; shows base detail.</p><p><strong>Wood</strong> — warmth contrast to PVD metal; specify edge sealing for humidity.</p><h2>Finish coordination</h2><p>Match PVD base to <a href="/studio/pvd-partitions">living room partition</a> and <a href="/shop/door-handles">handles</a> for cohesive open plans.</p><p>Finish guide: <a href="/blog/pvd-finish-selection-guide-gold-rose-gold-champagne-black">gold, rose gold, champagne, black</a>.</p><h2>Practical Indian living</h2><p>Tables receive trays, laptops and children\'s homework — avoid sharp glass corners in active family rooms or choose rounded tops.</p><p>Liftable tops or open base design help robot vacuums common in new urban homes pass underneath.</p><h2>Ordering custom tables</h2><p>Vyomika Atelier builds to your dimensions from our Delhi, India studio with delivery across India. International enquiries are reviewed project by project. Share sofa spec sheet, rug size and floor photos for proportion advice.</p><h2>Rug and floor finish context</h2><p>Dark PVD bases on light marble floors create strong focal contrast — ensure rug size still anchors seating group so table does not appear to float visually.</p><p>Polished stone floors show scratches from metal feet without protectors — specify felt or adjustable pads in order.</p><h2>Open-plan sight lines</h2><p>In open kitchen-living plans, coffee table finish should relate to island hardware and partition metal without matching every element exactly.</p><p>Lower profile bases preserve views through to garden or balcony — important in compact urban flats where vertical clutter accumulates quickly.</p><h2>Family and entertaining use</h2><p>Rounded corners on glass tops reduce injury risk in active family rooms. Removable trays on stone tops contain spills during entertaining.</p><p>Lift-top mechanisms are rare on bespoke metal tables but possible — discuss hinge clearance with sofa depth before specifying.</p><h2>Ordering and delivery practicalities</h2><p>Large stone tops may require crane or manual handling planning for upper floors — share access photos before delivery date.</p><p>International enquiries are reviewed project by project — dimensions and top material confirmed before quotation.</p><h2>Pairing with seating depth and cushion height</h2><p>Low deep sofas suit slightly lower table heights toward 400 mm; upright formal sofas tolerate 450 mm comfortably. Measure arm height when seated — arms should clear table edge when leaning back with a cup.</p><h2>Statement versus supporting role</h2><p>In minimalist rooms the coffee table may be the only sculptural object — a bold PVD base in champagne or black is justified. In richly patterned rooms with feature rugs and art, a quieter base lets other layers lead. Match role to brief before selecting base complexity.</p><h3>Nesting and secondary tables</h3><p>Large villas sometimes use a primary metal coffee table with smaller nested side tables in matching finish. Batch order nested sets together for colour consistency.</p><h2>Delivery access in urban towers</h2><p>Stone-topped tables may not fit in small service lifts — share lift cabin dimensions and corridor turn radii before fabrication. Split tops or site assembly may be required on upper floors without crane access.</p><h2>Material combinations that work in Indian living rooms</h2><p>Champagne PVD bases with grey or white marble tops suit neutral contemporary palettes common in Gurgaon and Bangalore high-rise apartments. Matte black bases with warm wood tops add contrast without competing with patterned rugs.</p><p>Glass tops showcase base sculpture but need regular underside dusting — specify tempered safety glass and rounded edges in family zones. Coordinate with <a href="/blog/pvd-furniture-care-finishes-customization">PVD furniture care</a> for long-term maintenance expectations.</p><h2>Styling with rugs and art</h2><p>Rug size should extend beyond chair front legs while leaving circulation paths clear — the table sits visually anchored within the rug field when proportions are correct. Oversized art above the sofa can balance a bold metal base without the table dominating the wall composition.</p><p>Review scale with a simple plan sketch before ordering custom dimensions — saves costly adjustments after delivery.</p><h2>Balancing metal with soft furnishings</h2><p>Heavy metal bases pair well with textured rugs and upholstered sofas that soften acoustic and visual hardness. If the room already uses much polished stone, a hairline champagne base may integrate more calmly than high-contrast black.</p><h2>Working with interior stylists</h2><p>Side tables in matching PVD finish can extend the seating group without competing with the main coffee table silhouette — specify as a set when visual unity matters.</p><h2>Lighting over the seating group</h2><p>Pendant height and coffee table surface interact visually — low pendants above a tall sculptural base can feel crowded. Review ceiling layout alongside table elevation before locking base height and top thickness in shop drawings.</p><p>Confirm lift access and corridor turning radii before ordering oversized stone tops — split delivery may be required on upper floors without service elevator capacity.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Choose a luxury metal coffee table by sofa proportion, base finish aligned with architectural metal, and top material suited to daily Indian living. The right table feels inevitable in the room — neither cramped nor floating in empty space.</p><p>Shop <a href="/shop/coffee-tables">coffee tables</a>.</p><p>Explore <a href="/shop/bespoke-metal-furniture">bespoke metal furniture</a>.</p><p>Care tips in <a href="/blog/pvd-furniture-care-finishes-customization">PVD furniture care</a>.</p><p>For a project-specific quotation, share floor plans or photos through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Architects and interior designers may also begin from the <a href="/professionals">professionals collaboration page</a>.</p>',
